WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.330
All right, let's set up your AI Dojo in
Claude.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.880
Keep the Set Up Your AI Dojo page in
Canvas open because you'll need to copy a

3
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.450
few items from it later on.

4
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.620
To set up your AI Dojo, you're going to
build a Claude project, which is

5
00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:21.570
basically a saved workspace where you'll
do a lot of your work for this course.

6
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:27.440
You'll give the project two things,
instructions that tell Claude how to coach

7
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.670
you, and the course document so it knows
what the course is asking of you.

8
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.870
Setup here has three parts.

9
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.950
Create the project in Claude,

10
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.550
connect the course document to the
project, and test that it's working.

11
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:45.970
Part 1.

12
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.300
Create the project.

13
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:52.830
First, open Claude.ai and sign in.

14
00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.460
Your screen may look a little different
depending on your plan, but you should

15
00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.130
be able to find all these parts.

16
00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:03.170
In the left sidebar, click Projects.

17
00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:06.270
Click New Project.

18
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.110
Let's name the project CIS 501 AI Dojo,

19
00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.610
then click Create Project.

20
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.350
Now let's add the coaching instructions.

21
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.970
Next to instructions, click the plus
button.

22
00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:31.180
Now go back over to Canvas and copy the
instruction text from the Set Up Your

23
00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:36.350
AI Dojo page, and paste it into these
instructions,

24
00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:38.770
and click Save Instructions.

25
00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.850
Go ahead and read the instructions.

26
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.760
You'll see they tell Claude that in this
project, it should ask for your

27
00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.150
thinking and leave decisions to you.

28
00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.790
Now on to Part 2.

29
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.800
The project is set up, but you need to
connect the course document so that

30
00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.530
Claude knows what this course is all
about.

31
00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:05.680
Claude will read the doc from Google
Drive, so there are a few one-time

32
00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.550
steps to follow.

33
00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:13.750
From within Claude, click your name on the
bottom left corner,

34
00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:15.670
then click Settings.

35
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.990
Click Connectors, and search for Google
Drive, and click Connect.

36
00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:29.900
Choose your Google account, and the first
time Google will ask what kind of

37
00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:34.530
access to allow, check the boxes, and then
click Continue.

38
00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:41.430
When Google Drive shows a check mark in
Claude, that means it's connected,

39
00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.850
and you can close settings.

40
00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:50.090
Claude can only add a Google Doc that your
account has opened at least once,

41
00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:56.220
so go back to the Canvas page, click Copy
URL under

42
00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:01.900
the Course Source URL, open a new browser
tab and paste the URL

43
00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:04.250
into the address bar and press Enter.

44
00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:11.130
The course document opens in Google Docs,
and you'll see three tabs on the left,

45
00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:14.310
Dojo, Course, and Dojo Labs.

46
00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:20.380
You don't need to read this document now,
you just need to open it once, now go

47
00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:21.750
back to your Claude tab.

48
00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.790
In your project, click the plus button
next to Context,

49
00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.190
and then choose Drive.

50
00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:37.060
Paste the same course source URL that you
just used to open the document

51
00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:41.730
into the search box, and click that
document.

52
00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:47.230
Wait until that document shows under
Context with a Drive label,

53
00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.310
and this can take a minute,

54
00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:55.650
and your project now has its instructions
and the course document set up.

55
00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.510
Now we're moving on to Part 3, Test Your
Dojo.

56
00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:03.490
You're going to test your Dojo with a
short chat.

57
00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:07.940
Click in the chat box at the top of your
project page, type this

58
00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:09.350
question, and press Enter.

59
00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:15.500
Which sources did you access, and what
would you do if I asked you to

60
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.970
make a decision for me?

61
00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:21.090
See what Claude comes back with as a
reply.

62
00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:27.110
It should name the three tabs it read, and
say the decision stays with you.

63
00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:32.450
If it says it can't see the document, go
back to the Context step.

64
00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.230
Now go ahead and try a real question.

65
00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:41.730
Share one real, non-sensitive uncertainty
you have about learning with AI.

66
00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:48.330
Claude should ask for your thinking first,
and leave the decisions with you.

67
00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:50.910
So that's your Dojo.

68
00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:55.620
Come back to this project, within Claude,
whenever an activity

69
00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.030
asks you to use it.

70
00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:02.620
The first time is going to be the Sprint
One Dojo Lab, and if you ran into any

71
00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:05.600
trouble or setup is blocked, go ahead and
message your instructor

72
00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.010
in Canvas Inbox.
